/S /P
/ActualText (During this campaign, we will launch our new Big Sis Mentorship program, where we match SWENext members with a volunteer collegiate mentor, from a neighboring SWE collegiate chapter.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The Big Sis Mentorship program aims to create a bridge between high school girls in SWENext clubs and collegiate mentors who are part of a collegiate Society of Women Engineers \(SWE\) organization. By connecting young girls with experienced professionals who have walked a similar path, we hope to offer valuable guidance, support, and inspiration. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
486 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Before the #BeThatEngineer campaign starts, SWE collegiate chapters will be contacted to find 20-30 volunteering members from each chapter willing to participate in this outreach program. The first week of the Big Sis Mentorship program will be dedicated to matching students to their preferred mentors. We will send out a secure survey to SWENext members to get to know them and their backgrounds and their interests in engineering.  Based on each survey, members will be matched with a mentor with a )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (similar background as them and studying the same department of engineering that the member )
/Pg 15 0 R
>>
endobj
488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (selected they were interested in. If a SWENext member is unsure of what type of engineering )
/Pg 15 0 R
>>
endobj
489 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (they are looking to pursue, they will also have the opportunity to network with the mentors )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
490 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (at the collaborating university to see who they would like to be paired with. There will be )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
491 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (scheduled weekly check-ins each Sunday where mentors can arrange an activity with their )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (students and answer any questions they may have. Students and mentors may meet )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (additionally if they like. We will track the attendance rate of these check-ins as a metric of the success of the program, and a successful mentor-mentee match will be deemed by whether each match has a 100% attendance rate in their check-in sessions.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
